# The blog was renamed to Notes. Nothing was widely linked at the time, but the
# old paths cost one line to honour and a 301 keeps any stray link alive.
/blog                /notes                301
/blog/*              /notes/:splat         301

# Intentionally no SPA catch-all.
#
# There used to be `/*  /index.html  200` here. Every route is static and known
# at build time, so tools/build-static.ts writes a real index.html for each one
# and the fallback is no longer needed to make deep links work.
#
# Keeping it would be actively harmful: it answered HTTP 200 for ANY path,
# including nonsense, so /whatever-you-type served the homepage with a success
# status. Search engines read that as unlimited duplicate pages, and genuinely
# dead links looked alive. Without it, Cloudflare Pages falls through to
# dist/404.html and returns a real 404.
#
# If a dynamic (non-prerenderable) route is ever added, give it its own rule
# here rather than restoring the blanket catch-all.
